pvai (0.5.30-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A prompt box in shell mode (it starts with "!", for example a command
    called back from the history) was taken for an unknown dialog: the
    session waited on a "screen" dialog that Esc could not close, and every
    new prompt only queued behind it. The wrapper now knows the shell box,
    reports it as a draft and never types a prompt into it.
  * Claude Code draws a no-break space after the "!" of shell mode; a box
    in shell mode is now recognised as the prompt box.
  * A prompt that starts with "!" (a shell command from the app) is
    delivered like a slash command: in once the box shows it, done with
    its output. Before, the box in shell mode looked like no prompt box,
    the prompt was taken back and pasted again on every retry.
  * New app command `clear` (and `pvai clear SESSION`): empties the prompt
    box wherever the cursor is and leaves shell mode (Ctrl+K, Ctrl+U,
    Backspace, a few at a time: Claude Code drops control keys that come
    in one large chunk); queued prompts go on once it is empty. Sessions
    say `clearable`.

